menu "CAN Bridge Example Configuration"

    config CAN_BRIDGE_SIMULATED_NODE
        bool "Simulate a CANopen DS402 node instead of using the TWAI peripheral"
        default n
        help
            Run a simulated CANopen (CiA 301) node with a CiA 402 drive profile
            in firmware instead of bridging to the TWAI (CAN) peripheral, so the
            hosted CAN console and DS402 panel web apps can be exercised with no
            transceiver, bus, or drive attached. The node answers NMT, serves
            the default SDO channel (expedited + segmented, with CiA 301 abort
            codes) from an object dictionary that includes its own stored EDS
            (0x1021), runs the DS402 state machine with profile position /
            velocity / torque and homing modes, sends a heartbeat and a TPDO,
            and raises an EMCY when a fault is injected (write 1 to 0x2000).
            The USB side of the bridge is unchanged: the web apps connect and
            talk to it exactly as they would with real hardware.

    config CAN_BRIDGE_SIMULATED_NODE_ID
        int "Simulated node id"
        depends on CAN_BRIDGE_SIMULATED_NODE
        range 1 127
        default 1
        help
            The CANopen node id (1..127) the simulated node answers on: SDO on
            0x600/0x580 + id, heartbeat on 0x700 + id, TPDO1 on 0x180 + id.

endmenu
